  "notes": "USAGE:\nA formal, literary word. The kanji {銘|めい} means \"inscription\" or \"engraving,\" so {銘記|めいき} literally suggests carving something into memory. Often used in speeches, essays, and formal writing.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {心|こころ}に{銘記|めいき}する (to engrave in one's heart)\n- {深|ふか}く{銘記|めいき}する (to remember deeply)\n- {銘記|めいき}すべき (worth keeping in mind)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {明記|めいき}: to state clearly in writing — same reading but different meaning (written documentation vs. mental remembrance)\n- {肝|きも}に{銘|めい}じる: to take to heart — similar meaning, also literary",
